From fbd9cccd69b1029b73ffa21ec23424cbc8b39c69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 17:03:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Build H.264 only, and advertise only what CreateConfig
 accepts

Two separate problems, both of which stop this branch being usable on a
6.18 kernel.

The build one: include/hevc-ctrls.h is a 2019 snapshot of HEVC controls
that have since been stabilized into linux/v4l2-controls.h. Every file
that includes it now redefines five structs the kernel headers already
define -- 5 errors across config.c, context.c and h265.c. PR #38 ported
H.264 to the stabilized uAPI and left HEVC on the old one, so h265.c
cannot compile against the new definitions either: it uses 3 of the 8
controls cedrus registers, and its sps/pps/slice_params/dpb_entry no
longer match field for field. Porting it is real work (see
docs/vaapi-scope.md); pretending it builds is not an option. So the
vestigial header is deleted and h265.c drops out of the build, staying in
the tree as the starting point for that port.

The honesty one: RequestCreateConfig already refuses MPEG-2 and HEVC --
that is what "Don't advertise broken profiles" did -- but
RequestQueryConfigProfiles still listed both. vainfo therefore reported
profiles that fail at vaCreateConfig, and vainfo is exactly the tool
used to decide whether this driver works at all. A decoder that
advertises what it cannot do pushes the failure onto its caller. The
advertised set is now H.264 and nothing else, matching what the driver
will actually do.
